xpad version 1.4 README
-------------------------

xpad is a virtual sticky pad system using GTK+ 2.

Caution: Once you have run xpad 1.4, older xpad versions may not work
	properly.  But, why would you want to go back?  :)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
INSTALLATION NOTES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
     To compile, just type "make" and / or "make install".

     Read the INSTALL file for more.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
USAGE NOTES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
     Right click to obtain configuration options and open new pads.

     Hold down CTRL and left-click drag to move a pad.  Hold down CTRL and 
		right-drag to resize a pad.

     Add xpad to your ~/.xinitrc to have xpad start with every X boot.

     xpad stores its files in ~/.xpad.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
COMMAND ARGUMENTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
	Standard GTK+ arguments are understood.  In addition, the following
		arguments are available.

	--help, -h:			Prints usage information and exits.

	--version, -V:		Prints version information and exits.

	--verbosity=%i, -v:	Where %i is the amount of output you desire.
				0 is none; 1 is moderate; 2 is debug.  
				Default is 0
	
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
KNOWN BUGS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
	None!

